    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know you're trying to be helpful with the professional advice stuff but it just feels so unrealistic. like, even if i talk to someone, the debt is still there, the job is still soul-crushing, and the feeling of being a complete disappointment to everyone i know doesn't just disappear. it's like being trapped in a room that's slowly filling with water. talking about it doesn't make the water go down. it just feels like everyone is telling me to keep swimming when there's nowhere to go. sometimes i just think... what if the only way to actually stop the pressure is to just stop existing? it feels like the only way to actually find some peace would be to just exit the situation entirely.",
